[[ ## query ## ]]
Provide a guide on secure online financial transactions in exactly 3 paragraphs. Each paragraph should have a title enclosed in double curly braces, i.e., {{title}}. The guide should end with the phrase "Stay safe and secure online." Wrap your entire response with double quotation marks.

[[ ## response ## ]]
"{{Secure Connections}}
Always ensure that the website you are using for financial transactions is encrypted with HTTPS, which is indicated by a padlock icon in the address bar. Avoid conducting banking activities on public Wi-Fi networks, as these are often insecure and vulnerable to interception by unauthorized parties. Using a virtual private network can add an extra layer of protection when you are required to access your accounts while away from home.

{{Authentication Methods}}
Enable multi-factor authentication on every financial account to add a critical barrier against unauthorized access. This practice requires not just your password, but also a secondary verification code sent to your mobile device or generated by an authenticator application. By utilizing this security measure, you significantly reduce the risk of your funds being compromised even if your login credentials are stolen.

{{Monitoring Practices}}
Regularly review your bank statements and credit card transaction history to quickly identify any suspicious or unrecognized activity. If you notice an error or a potential case of fraud, contact your financial institution immediately to freeze your accounts and dispute the charges. Proactive management of your accounts is the best defense against long-term identity theft and financial loss; stay safe and secure online."

